    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In the Visayas, a frontier island grid facing new pressures, grid pioneers are navigating uncharted demand. The crisis was triggered by an unexpected unit failure revealing system vulnerabilities: a power plant unit tripped offline, creating a massive power shortfall challenging grid stability. This challenge intensified as a series of generator failures testing system limits coincided with a heatwave pushing grid into uncharted demand territory. In response, decision-makers exploring crisis options implemented emergency measures to navigate the crisis, triggering a high-stakes grid alert.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
